On Tuesday, May 07, 2013 23:24:08 Lee Carlson wrote:
> fi'i je'e (I hope that I'm correctly expressing thankful understanding). So
> "roda roroi binxo" will suffice?

Do you mean "binxo" or "cenba"? Translating "change" into Lojban is often 
tricky.

I would say "lo nu cenba po'o cu stodi" or "no na'ebo lo nu cenba cu stodi".

Btw, "fi'i" is "welcome" in the sense of "Welcome to my humble abode". "Thank 
you" is "ki'e do", which is answered with "je'e".

